# Code That Runs Before the Response

Middleware allows you to execute code **before** a request is completed.

It sits at the edge (closer to the user) and can modify the response, redirect, rewrite, or add headers.

You create a `middleware.js` (or `.ts`) file at the root of your project (same level as `pages` or `app`).

```js
// middleware.js
export function middleware(request) {
  // Your logic here
}
```

It intercepts every incoming request and can decide what to do.

slides.codeSnippet:
// middleware.js
import { NextResponse } from 'next/server';

export function middleware(request) {
  if (request.nextUrl.pathname.startsWith('/old-blog')) {
    return NextResponse.redirect(new URL('/blog', request.url));
  }
  // Continue to the requested page
  return NextResponse.next();
}

